      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "HO3 (dynamic reprioritization) requires new concerning symptoms after an initial low-risk plan is established. Although the caregiver later reports morning stability with no seizures or bleeding, no new emergent red flag (e.g., black stool, hematemesis, unresponsive repetitive speech) emerged to require a change in urgency. The initial plan already included emergency escalation thresholds.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
